! mcp_bootstrap_p127.strap -- the TAPE MOUNT / SPACE / WRITE-EOF exits,
! the CM interrupt-class decoder and the SUPPRESS / WAIT entries,
! printed page 127.  docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.134, header READ
! and not assumed: "TIME CLOCK 00054041 ... DIST. OF 3/01   3/01
! PAGE NUMBER  127", and the header's own "LOCATION 216171" names the
! page's first word.
!
! FIFTY-SIX LINES, ALL OF THEM CODE.  216171.00 .. 216240.00, with
! no gap anywhere: every row's location is the previous row's plus
! one half word or one full word, checked row by row.  Nothing is
! reserved, nothing is a SYN, nothing is a comment card.  One VF
! (line 1) and fifty-five instructions.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CARD SERIAL COLUMN, AND THE ONE THING IT FOUND
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! x=4608..4850 at 300 dpi, rendered at 600 dpi.  The serials run
! EB000245 (line 1) .. EB000299 (line 56): FIFTY-FIVE CARDS FOR
! FIFTY-SIX LINES.  They are strictly consecutive -- line n is
! EB000(244+n) -- through line 54 (EB000298), and then
!
!   line 55  LV,$0,STIC            EB000299
!   line 56  SV,$0,SINTAD($13)     EB000299
!
! carry THE SAME SERIAL.  That is STRAP's semicolon: one card
! punched "LV,$0,STIC ; SV,$0,SINTAD($13)".  printed p.120 found the
! identical idiom twice on its own page and C22-6728 prints it in
! prose as "(SIC,STIC; B,SIFAD)".  The deck writes the two halves on
! two lines, which assembles identically; the card fact is recorded
! here and nowhere else.  There is no restart and no second
! doubling: the column is one unbroken EB run, so nothing fell off
! the top or the bottom of the render.
!
! THE PREFIX HAS CHANGED SINCE THE LAST TRANSCRIBED PAGE.  printed
! p.120 punched EA000149..EA000161; this page punches EB0002nn.  A
! new punched deck therefore starts somewhere in the untranscribed
! pp.121-126, and whoever takes those pages should look for the
! restart in the serial column -- printed p.103 got a real finding
! out of exactly this signal (a CA000001 restart that marked a
! SECOND COPY of the communication region).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHERE IT SITS -- AND THE PAGE PRINTS NO SLC
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THERE IS NO SLC ROW ON THIS PAGE. <<<  Line 1 is already a VF
! at 216171.00, so the counter ARRIVES there.  The "SLC,(8)216171.00"
! below therefore ASSERTS the origin and cannot check it (printed
! p.111's agent measured that a hard SLC overrides the arriving
! counter silently and all its rows still pass).  The join was
! compared BY HAND against the two neighbours, neither of which is
! transcribed yet, using docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt:
!
!   BACKWARD.  printed p.126 line 56 is
!     "216170.40   215762.10 00   B,K G IN"
!   a half-word branch, so the counter leaves p.126 at 216171.00.
!   Exactly this page's first location.  (printed p.125 line 38 and
!   printed p.126 line 54 also reference K CS Q -- "LV,11,K CS Q"
!   prints 216171.26 and "SV,11,K CS Q" prints 216171.27 -- and
!   printed p.125 line 37 and p.126 lines 50 and 52 print
!   "KCSQ+.31" as 216171.37.  Five more witnesses that word 216171
!   is K CS Q.)
!
!   FORWARD.  printed p.128 line 1 is
!     "216240.40   215762.34 C0   BZRZ,K G IN"
!   and this page's last row, line 56, is a half word at 216240.00.
!   216240.00 + 0.40 = 216240.40.  The trail is contiguous in both
!   directions.
!
!   AND THE TWO NEIGHBOURS BRANCH TO THE SAME WORD BY DIFFERENT
!   OPS, which is the best evidence on this page for the byte
!   dispute below: K G IN is at 215762.00, p.126 line 56 reaches it
!   with "B" and prints "215762.10 00", p.128 line 1 reaches it with
!   "BZRZ" and prints "215762.34 C0".  Same target, same page band,
!   read by tesseract rather than by eye -- and the B is 00 while
!   the BZRZ is C0, exactly as lines 21 and 23 of this page print.
!
! TAIL SCOPE.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the
! origin here, and pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the "TAIL,(2)G" block that
! printed p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed with
! "UNTAIL,(2)".  Two of this page's externals have T-prefixed twins
! inside that block, at the SAME offsets, and that is tail scope and
! NOT a collision:
!   S SYSTM 000007.31  vs  "T SYSTM SYN(BU,1),7.25"
!   S REEL K 000010.71 vs  "T REELK SYN(BU,7),8.57"
! both on printed p.84 lines 50 and 52 (OCR'd PDF p.91).  The T
! twins even print the same instruction: printed p.90 line 25
! (OCR'd PDF p.97) is "CM1111,TSYSTM(TMXE)" compiling
! "000007.31 86  001000.36 F0",
! which is this page's line 8 with a different index register.
! Recorded, not "fixed".
!
! A THIRD TAIL-SCOPE REPEAT, THIS ONE ON A NAME THIS DECK SYNs.
! tests/check_symbol_spellings.py reports zero disagreements with
! this deck added, but it does show SLRBU at TWO addresses:
! 215324.00 here (and in printed p.117's deck) and 0o2155.00 in
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p19/p28/p29.strap.  printed p.117's own
! header already states that case -- those pages are INSIDE the
! TAIL,(2)G block, so it is tail scope and not a collision.  None
! of the fourteen names THIS page defines appears anywhere else in
! the corpus at any address.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE CONTAINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 1-15   K CS Q and the MOUNT / NO-SYSTEM / RELEASE exits.
!              K CS Q is a one-word VF,0 cell (the CS queue head);
!              K MOUNT bumps the current-reel pointer and the reel
!              count in the unit area table, tests SYSTAP (SYSTEM
!              TAPE, printed p.108 line 11) and sets or clears
!              S VER / S SYSTM accordingly before branching to
!              K FAKE on printed p.126.
! Lines 16-27  K SPACE / K FORWD / K WEF: space a file forward or
!              back (M+1 and M-1 on S FILE K), write an end-of-file
!              (KI(BU,8),79 -- 79 is the EOF control code), and the
!              KI(BU,8),(8)176 above it.
! Lines 28-37  CMINTP, the interrupt-class decoder.  Its own comment
!              is the oracle for the four mnemonics under it:
!              "-CHECK FOR OP,AD,USA OR DS" names, in order, B OP Z,
!              B AD Z, B USA Z, B DS Z -- lines 30, 31, 32, 33.
!              Line 29's comment is "-EXE SHOULD BE OFF AT THIS
!              POINT".  CMINTZ then sets a count of 15 and transmits
!              fifteen words from S TLR to S LR BU.
! Lines 38-47  K SUPRS / C NOWAT / C WAIT: save the IC in S IC BU
!              and S INT AD, branch on the program-status-table bits
!              S SIO (SUPPRESSED MODE STATUS, printed p.109 line 10)
!              and S AS (AUTO STACK STATUS, printed p.109 line 8).
! Lines 48-52  C JUMP: transmit the limit registers for the PP or
!              the MCP and go to K SERCH.
! Lines 53-56  KFREE: clear the copied-control-word bit, test
!              $7.37 (comment "-EPGK,LK, OR EE ON"), and save the
!              stored IC.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE EIGHTEEN SYMBOLS THIS PAGE REFERENCES AND DOES NOT DEFINE,
! PLUS THIRTEEN TABLE OFFSETS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EVERY SPELLING BELOW COMES FROM A DEFINING CARD, NOT FROM THIS
! PAGE'S INK.  Nine are already landed in decks/ and are copied
! verbatim, data description and all; four more were found as
! defining cards in the volume OCR; the absolute ones were found as
! LABEL rows in the volume OCR.  Said here because the brief asks
! for it to be said.
!
! TABLE OFFSETS -- written BARE DECIMAL, exactly as their own
! defining cards and the landed decks write them.  These are indexed
! operands ($3/$9/$11/$12/$13), and because the whole 24-bit
! word.bit pair lands in the instruction's address field, a VFL or
! branch-on-bit reference pins them EXACTLY -- there is no half-word
! ambiguity for these.
!   SYSTAP  SYN(BU,1), .27      decks/mcp_bootstrap_p108.strap, line 11
!   SAS     SYN(BU,1), .25      decks/mcp_bootstrap_p109.strap, line  8
!   SSIO    SYN(BU,1), .61      decks/mcp_bootstrap_p109.strap, line 10
!   SSYSTM  SYN(BU,1), 7.25     decks/mcp_bootstrap_p101.strap, line 23
!   SFILEK  SYN(BU,12), 7.38    decks/mcp_bootstrap_p101.strap, line 25
!   SREELK  SYN(BU,7), 8.57     decks/mcp_bootstrap_p101.strap, line 27
!   SCREEL  SYN(BU,18), 8.32    decks/mcp_bootstrap_p101.strap, line 28
!   SINTAD  SYN(BU,19), 1.32    decks/mcp_bootstrap_p102.strap, line  8
!   SCCW    SYN(BU,64), 4.0     decks/mcp_bootstrap_p102.strap, line 15
!   SSETUP  SYN(BU,1), 0.31     printed p.99 line 25, OCR'd PDF p.106:
!                               "000000.37+  BU,01 ,10  S SET UP
!                                SYN(BU,1),0.31 -PSEUDO-OP SET-UP,
!                                UNIT STATUS BIT"
!   SVER    SYN(BU,1), 0.40     printed p.99 line 32, OCR'd PDF p.106:
!                               "000000.50+ ... S VER SYN(BU,1),0.40
!                                -VERIFY FILE STATUS"
!   SRD     SYN(BU,1), 0.57     printed p.99 line 45, OCR'd PDF p.106:
!                               "000000.71+ ... S RD SYN(BU,1),0.57
!                                -READ, OPERATION STATUS"
!   SWR     SYN(BU,1), 0.58     printed p.99 line 46, OCR'd PDF p.106:
!                               "000000.72+ ... S WR SYN(BU,1),0.58
!                                -WRITE, OPERATION STATUS"
!
! >>> THE WEAKEST FOUR, NAMED SO THEY GET RE-COMPARED. <<<  S VER,
! S SET UP, S RD and S WR are the only externals here with NO landed
! deck behind them: printed p.99 is not transcribed, so they rest on
! the volume OCR of that page alone.  Their VALUES are solid -- the
! OCR'd resolved LOCATION column reads 000000.50+, 000000.37+,
! 000000.71+ and 000000.72+, which is exactly what this page's rows
! 7/10, 13, 17 and 16 compile against -- but the "(BU,1)" MODES come
! only from the garbled data-description column, and no row here
! inherits one of them (every row that uses them prints its own
! "(BU,1)" or is a branch-on-bit), so nothing on this page would
! notice if a mode were wrong.  RE-COMPARE THESE FOUR WHEN p.99
! LANDS.
!
! >>> THE DATA DESCRIPTIONS ON THOSE SYNs ARE LOAD-BEARING HERE, AND
! THEY ARE NOT DECORATION. <<<  Three of this page's rows carry NO
! data description of their own and inherit the symbol's:
!   line  3  "M+1,S REEL K($12)"  -> second half word 007000.22 B0
!   line  8  "CM1111,SSYSTM($12)" -> second half word 001000.36 F0
!   line 20  "M+1,S FILE K($12)"  -> second half word 014000.22 B0
! 0o007000, 0o001000 and 0o014000 are the LENGTH fields 7, 1 and 12,
! i.e. SYN(BU,7), SYN(BU,1) and SYN(BU,12).  Written without the
! data description the same rows compile 000000.22 B0 and miss by
! the whole length field.  The three !CHECK rows below are what
! verifies the three inherited descriptions.
!
! ABSOLUTE EXTERNALS -- (8) style, as printed pp.117 and 120 write
! theirs.  Every one has an OCR'd LABEL ROW at the stated address;
! the branch that references it here pins only bit 18 (the ".00" or
! ".40"), so the label row is what supplies the rest.
! Each citation below is PRINTED page (OCR'd PDF page), checked
! against the OCR file's own page markers and not assumed.
!   KFAKE   216160.00  printed p.126 line 46 (PDF 133): "216160.00
!                      K FAKE  CM0000(BU,1),S REW($11)"
!   KSTACK  215742.00  printed p.122 line 42 (PDF 129): "215742.00
!                      K STACK  BB,S RD($11),K COPY"   (this row also
!                      independently witnesses S RD = 000000.71)
!   KCOPY   215744.00  printed p.122 line 45 (PDF 129): "215744.00
!                      K COPY  CCW,0.0($14),S CCW($13)"
!   KGATE   215746.40  printed p.123 line  1 (PDF 130): "215746.40
!                      K GATE  BZB,SUNSLP($11),..."
!   KILEGL  220064.00  printed p.160 (PDF 167): "220064.00  K ILEGL
!                      LCI,7,(8)400"
!   KSUPP   216242.00  printed p.128 line  2 (PDF 135): "216242.00
!                      K SUPP  NOP,K COMM"
!   KCOMM   216004.40  printed p.123 line 42 (PDF 130): "216004.40
!                      K COMM  BB,S M,$+2.32"
!                      (that row also witnesses S M = 215001.05)
!   KUNSTC  222037.00  printed p.198 line 36 (PDF 205): "222037.00
!                      K UNSTC  LVI,9,S PROG S"
!   KNINTY  216010.00  printed p.123 line 48 (PDF 130): "216010.00
!                      K NINTY  B,K UNSTC"
!                      -- and that row compiles 222037.10 00, which
!                      is this page's line 37 bit for bit.  Note
!                      K NINTY at 216010.00 and K INT TY at
!                      216010.40 are TWO different labels one half
!                      word apart; line 47's "LVI,1,K NINTY" prints
!                      216010.03, bit 18 clear, so it is the former.
!   KSERCH  222020.00  printed p.198 line  5 (PDF 205): "222020.00
!                      K SERCH  LVI,9,S PROG S"
!   STLR    215230.00  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p117.strap, verbatim
!   SLRBU   215324.00  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p117.strap, verbatim
!   SLRMCP  215362.00  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p117.strap, verbatim
!   SL      215001.04  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p117.strap, verbatim
!   STIC    215265.00  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p110/111/112/117, verbatim
!   SM      215001.05  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap "!SYM SM
!                      215001.05" ("S M SYN(BU,1),S COM RG+0.05")
!   SLRPP   215266.00  NEW HERE as a SYN.  printed p.116's deck
!                      header already states the layout from that
!                      page's own ink -- "S LR PP 215266.00..215322
!                      then S IC PP 215323.00 / S LR BU 215324.00 /
!                      S LR MCP 215362.00" -- and lines 49 and 51
!                      here print 215266.36 and 215362.36 against
!                      line 35's 215324.36, the three in step.
!   SICBU   215361.00  NEW HERE as a SYN.  Same p.116 header:
!                      "S LR BU 215324.00..215360 then S IC BU
!                      215361.00".
!
! >>> THE INDEX-INSTRUCTION OPERANDS ARE PINNED ONLY TO THE HALF
! WORD. <<<  STLR, SLRBU, SLRPP, SLRMCP, SICBU, STIC, SCREEL and
! SINTAD are reached by LV / SV / T, whose 6-bit octal field is the
! OPERATION code plus bit 18 of the operand, not the operand's bit
! offset.  Measured on this page: LV,n prints 2n in that field and
! SV,n prints 2n+1, so line 2's "LV,3,S C REEL($12)" prints
! 000010.46 = 0o40 + 0o06 and line 5's SV prints 000010.47.  Only
! the 0o40 is address.  Writing ".00" for the others is a
! CONVENTION and no !CHECK can test it.  S C REEL is the exception
! and the proof: its defining card on printed p.101 line 28 says
! "SYN(BU,18),8.32", bit 32 = 0o40, which is exactly what the
! half-word bit demanded.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE INK, WHERE IT MATTERED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THIS PAGE OPENS ROUND GLYPHS CONSTANTLY AND ITS OWN HEADING
! PRINTS "LOCATICN". <<<  Line 11's second half word prints
! "001000.CC FO" for 001000.00 F0 and line 9 prints "216161.1C CO"
! for 216161.10 00, so an open glyph here carries almost no
! information.  Three places where that had to be settled on
! something other than shape:
!
! 1. THE "FC" THAT IS F0.  Lines 10, 13 and 36 print their second
!    half word's trailing byte with an open first glyph.  It is F0:
!    decks/mcp_bootstrap_p117.strap line 45 is the IDENTICAL
!    statement "CM1111(BU,1),S L" and its landed, verified !CHECK
!    reads "215001.04 80 001000.36 F0" -- the same word this page's
!    line 36 prints.  Lines 7 and 10 are also the same statement as
!    each other and must compile the same bits.
!
! 2. LINES 23 AND 45 ARE "C0" AND THE INK CANNOT SAY SO.  At 1800
!    dpi line 21 ("B,K STACK", which the assembler and the oracle
!    both make 00) prints its byte with the SAME open first glyph as
!    line 23 ("BZRZ,K GATE").  So shape is exhausted, and "I looked
!    again and it is a C" is not available.  What settles it is the
!    MNEMONIC, against landed checks on other pages:
!       215476.00  215627.32 C0   BZXE,M NO MCP
!       215477.40  215630.74 C0   BZRZ,M OP CI
!       005017.40  005402.34 C0   BZRZ,T MREJ
!    and the WELL-INKED octal field beside the byte agrees with
!    those exactly: BZXE prints .32 to a word-aligned target (line
!    45, C NOWAT at 216225.00) and BZRZ prints .34 + 0o40 = .74 to a
!    half-word target (line 23, K GATE at 215746.40).  So the
!    !CHECK on lines 23 and 45 TESTS THE MNEMONIC READING; it does
!    not independently confirm the byte.  Line 45 has a second
!    reading (the volume OCR reads "216225.32 CO"); LINE 23 HAS
!    NONE -- the OCR of this page jumps from line 21 to line 24 and
!    drops lines 22 and 23 entirely.
!
! 3. "K CS Q" HAS A Q.  At 1200 dpi the fourth glyph carries the
!    descender tail.  Confirmed independently by printed p.126,
!    whose lines 38 and 54 print "LV,11,K CS Q" and "SV,11,K CS Q".
!
! THE INDEX NIBBLE IS AN INTERNAL CHECK AND IT HELD ON EVERY ROW.
! The low nibble of a VFL half word is the index register: line 7's
! ($11) prints 8B, line 8's ($12) prints 8C, line 39's ($13) prints
! 3D, line 41's ($9) prints 89, line 4's ($3) prints 33.  Fifty-six
! rows, no exception.
!
! SPELLINGS SETTLED BY THE COMMENT COLUMN OR BY ANOTHER PAGE:
!   S RD      line 17, printed "SRD($11)" -- C or D is undecidable
!             at 400 dpi.  It is D: printed p.122's K STACK row
!             prints the identical first half word 000000.71 8B for
!             "BB,S RD($11),K COPY", and printed p.99 line 45
!             defines "S RD ... -READ, OPERATION STATUS".
!   S SIO     line 41.  Read S-I-O at 1800 dpi and confirmed by
!             decks/mcp_bootstrap_p109.strap, which landed
!             "SSIO SYN(BU,1), .61  -SUPPRESSED MODE STATUS" at
!             000000.75 after reading that page's own English.
!   $IND      line 28, printed "$INC" to the eye and to tesseract.
!             It is $IND, the indicator register (word 0o13): the
!             row's comment is "-CHECK FOR OP,AD,USA OR DS" and the
!             four rows under it branch on indicators.
!   CMINTP /  lines 28 and 34 print with NO space, unlike this
!   CMINTZ    page's other C-prefixed labels (C NOWAT, C WAIT,
!             C JUMP).  Recorded; it changes no symbol, because
!             STRAP ignores blanks inside a name.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ONE ASSEMBLER GAP, NAMED BY MECHANISM
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> A WRITTEN-MINUS VFL FORM WITH NO DATA DESCRIPTION IS REJECTED.
! <<<  Line 22 prints "M-1,SFILEK($12)" -- bare, exactly as line 20
! prints "M+1,S FILE K($12)" -- and strap_asm says
!
!   unknown mnemonic 'M-1' (not a supported instruction or pseudo-op)
!
! The mechanism: strap_asm.py applies opcodes.VFL_INT_WRITTEN_MINUS
! ("M-1" -> "M+1" plus invert, "-MG" -> "+MG" plus invert) only
! INSIDE the "if dds:" branch (around line 1536).  A form with no
! data description never reaches that rewrite and falls through to
! the unknown-mnemonic error, even though M+1 in the identical
! position resolves fine and inherits S FILE K's own SYN(BU,12).
! "-MG" sits in the same table and has the same shape, so it would
! fail the same way.
!
! THE DECK WRITES "M-1(BU,12), SFILEK($12)", which is BIT-IDENTICAL
! -- measured: both forms give 000007.46 8C 014000.32 B0, the
! printed word -- and the printed form is kept in the !CHECK note.
! This is a substitution and it is flagged as one.  The reading
! itself is not in doubt: opcodes.py's own note records that M-1's
! second half word differs from M+1's by 0o10 (".32 B0" against
! ".22 B0"), and that is exactly the difference printed between
! lines 20 and 22.
!
! NOTHING ELSE WAS SUBSTITUTED.  The printed "CM1111,SSYSTM($12)"
! (line 8, no data description) was TESTED before being touched and
! strap_asm accepts it and compiles it bit-exactly, so it stands as
! printed.  So do "KI(BU,8),(8)176", "LCI,$15,30.0", "L(BU,3),$7.37"
! and "CT0011(BU,5),$IND+.15".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT IS CHECKED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! All fourteen defined symbols against the LOCATION column, and ALL
! FIFTY-SIX rows against the BINARY OUTPUT column.  Nothing on this
! page is a DRZ or a SYN, so there is no row the convention asks to
! leave out.
!
! WHAT THE CHECKS CANNOT SEE, restated for this page: the SLC is
! asserted and not checked (see the join note above); the index-
! instruction externals are pinned only to the half word; and the
! bytes on lines 23 and 45 rest on the mnemonic, not on this page's
! ink.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

! -- table offsets, bare decimal, verbatim from their defining cards
